One-time main/production SHA-alignment trigger: deploy the exact merged main commit after the documentation-only observation-gate updates. The existing production-deploy workflow must pass the complete test suite before deploying and verify /health git_sha equals GITHUB_SHA. Runtime source behavior, D1 schema/data, source list, circuit policy (three consecutive transient failures, 15-minute initial cooldown, exponential backoff up to six hours), Retry-After handling for HTTP 429, and AUTH_REQUIRED treatment for 401/403 remain unchanged. No migration or direct D1 data write is part of this deployment.

Production rollout for the approved demand-index/duplicate-race release: after PR #186 merges, the path-triggered production-deploy workflow must test the exact merged main SHA, deploy that SHA, and verify /health git_sha before any D1 migration workflow is considered. This trigger does not authorize or execute a D1 write; migration 0007 remains a separate founder-approved, guarded workflow.

Production rollout for the AgentJob inclusive 60-second gate boundary fix and dynamic 0007 preflight: the production-deploy workflow must run the complete test suite, deploy this exact merged main commit, and verify /health git_sha equals GITHUB_SHA before the guarded 0007 workflow is allowed to write. The 0007 workflow independently waits for that same SHA and a subsequent COMPLETED growth cycle with four source rows. This trigger authorizes only deployment of the tested Worker; it does not authorize D1 SQL, schema changes, deletion, or restore.


Production rollout for PR #190: deploy merged main with the Cloudflare internal _cf_* D1 inventory exclusion. The deployment workflow must pass the full test suite and verify /health git_sha exactly equals this commit. The same main commit also activates the separately allowlisted 0007 workflow; it must wait for that deployed SHA and a fresh eligible COMPLETED cycle before capturing a same-run bookmark and executing only migrations/0007_demand_query_indexes.sql.
